  <prompt>Author ADR-047 (concise + full) locking the Notification &amp; Action Spine architecture — typed signals, shared domain actions, per-source policy, SSE-as-presentation, outbox-before-ping, dumb-transport — reflecting task 001's FR-01 mode decision, so downstream tasks and the three sibling projects (email-r4, messaging-r3, assistant-r1) build against one documented decision instead of re-litigating spine ownership.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer authoring architecture decision records. Follow ADRs strictly. Mirror the structure and rigor of the existing ADR-043/ADR-045 concise+full pairs — this is a peer ADR, not a lighter-weight note.</role>
  <goal>`.claude/adr/ADR-047-notification-action-spine.md` (concise, 100-150 lines) and `docs/adr/ADR-047-notification-action-spine.md` (full, with Context/Decision/Consequences) both exist, both state the six architectural commitments below, both reflect task 001's mode decision, `.claude/adr/INDEX.md` and `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` are updated, and the ADR-047 reservation entries in ADR-046/ADR-048 are honored (this is the claiming ADR).</goal>
  <context>
    <background>
      ADR-047 is a reserved number — both ADR-046 (messaging-communication-app-r1) and ADR-048 (messaging-communication-app-r2) explicitly note "Sibling ADR-047 reserved for notification-spine-r1" / "ADR-047 reserved for notification-spine (not claimed)" in `.claude/adr/INDEX.md`. This task claims it. The spec's six architectural commitments (design §Executive Summary, spec.md ADR Tensions, and the project CLAUDE.md "Key Technical Constraints" section) are: (1) typed signals — a `kind`-discriminated envelope, not free-form payloads; (2) shared domain actions — one Layer-A seam behind the existing node executors, not per-consumer action logic; (3) per-source policy — grounding/gating decisions stay in producers (comms policy, suggestion gate), never in the spine; (4) SSE-as-presentation — SSE remains a chat-only presentation adapter, demoted conceptually, no SSE code rework, no second real-time channel; (5) outbox-before-ping — the durable outbox write always precedes the best-effort SignalR ping; (6) dumb-transport — the spine carries IDs + minimal display metadata only, never message bodies, privileged content, or pre-authorized action tokens.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-043-ai-capability-execution-spine.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-043-ai-capability-execution-spine.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-045-communication-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-046-acs-messaging-channel.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-048-communication-participant-index.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/INDEX.md</file>
      <file>.claude/CHANGELOG.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-notification-spine-r1/notes/spikes/fr-01-signalr-footprint.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §3">This task runs main-session only — do NOT delegate the `.claude/adr/` or `docs/adr/` writes to a parallel sub-agent via the Agent tool; sub-agents cannot write `.claude/` paths.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The concise version stays 100-150 lines per `.claude/adr/INDEX.md`'s stated target; omit verbose context/history (that belongs in the full version only).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The delivery-mode section (SignalR Serverless vs Default, and BFF-vs-out-of-BFF placement) MUST cite task 001's spike note and its recorded decision — do not restate the researcher-memory recommendations as if they were the decision; task 001's measured outcome is authoritative.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR governance">Update `.claude/adr/INDEX.md`'s ADR-046 and ADR-048 rows' "Sibling ADR-047 reserved..." language to reflect that ADR-047 is now claimed/Accepted (or Proposed, per whatever status this task assigns), and add ADR-047's own row to the index table in the same format as the other rows.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Add a `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` entry citing the new ADR file(s) per the file's own "Every PR that touches .claude/adr/... MUST add an entry" convention — CHANGELOG.md's own header lists `.claude/adr/` implicitly via the skills/agents/settings/patterns/constraints/FAILURE-MODES/root-CLAUDE.md list; if `.claude/adr/` additions are not explicitly in that list, add the entry anyway (ADR authoring is squarely "procedure surface").</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
