    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="concise+full ADR pair" location=".claude/adr/ADR-043-ai-capability-execution-spine.md + docs/adr/ADR-043-ai-capability-execution-spine.md">Concise = Status/Domain/Builds-on header, Decision, Constraints (MUST/MUST NOT with code-pattern examples), Integration. Full = adds Deciders, Context (the "why" narrative with cited evidence), and cross-references back to the concise version.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read task 001's spike note (`notes/spikes/fr-01-signalr-footprint.md`) for the mode/placement decision; if the file does not exist or has no recorded decision, fire the escalation trigger below instead of proceeding.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `.claude/adr/ADR-043-ai-capability-execution-spine.md` and its full-version counterpart as the structural template; read ADR-045/046/048 for how adjacent communication-architecture ADRs are framed (ADR-047 is adjacent, not overlapping, per spec §ADR Tensions).</step>
    <step order="3">Draft `.claude/adr/ADR-047-notification-action-spine.md` (concise): Decision section states the six commitments (typed signals, shared domain actions, per-source policy, SSE-as-presentation, outbox-before-ping, dumb-transport) as MUST/MUST NOT rules with short code/contract examples; a delivery-mode subsection cites task 001's decision.</step>
    <step order="4">Draft `docs/adr/ADR-047-notification-action-spine.md` (full): add Context (why a shared spine — the "each consumer forks its own push mechanism" failure mode this project prevents, citing email-r4/messaging-r3/assistant-r1 as the three would-be forks), Deciders, and a Consequences section noting the R3 contract-lock dependency (FR-19) and the Notification-flip ADR-043 tension (Path C, comply-sequenced) already resolved in spec.md.</step>
    <step order="5">Update `.claude/adr/INDEX.md`: add ADR-047's row; update the ADR-046 and ADR-048 rows' reservation language to reflect ADR-047 is now authored.</step>
    <step order="6">Add a `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` → Added entry for the new ADR-047 files.</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to completed.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-notification-spine-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the spike (task 001) is not yet resolved — no spike note, or the spike note has no explicit go/no-go and mode decision — do not finalize the delivery-mode section of ADR-047; escalate and pause this task rather than guessing at the mode.</trigger>
  </escalation>
